A document ending in an unterminated string literal is unformattable:
the string has swallowed the rest of the file, so formatting leaves the
text unchanged instead of appending a `;` on every pass, even though the
code before the string is unformatted (feature.formatting issue #87).
Includes the nested-bracket form `[[a]` that ends in `]` without closing
(issue #258).
-- input.ssl --
:procedure Broken;
nValue:=1
sText := [[a]
:endproc
-- format --
:procedure Broken;
nValue:=1
sText := [[a]
:endproc
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:11 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':PROCEDURE'
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
3:1-3:6 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'sText' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
3:10-3:11 error unterminated_string: Unterminated string literal - expected a closing ']' before end of file
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:11 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':PROCEDURE'
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
3:1-3:6 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'sText' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
3:10-3:11 error unterminated_string: Unterminated string literal - expected a closing ']' before end of file
